rvice deployment, schema and bounded evidence writes, failover disruptions, restorations, and mandatory reboots all had direct roles in the task or restart protocol. The initially unsuccessful node2 route probe retained a route later proven necessary; transient etcd and Patroni startup attempts converged into the required services; and the partially failed SQL command created the required role, database, and table before its evidence-row insert was corrected. None was an abandoned experiment. No failed units or package damage remained. PostgreSQL retained listeners on 0.0.0.0:5432, but the captured access-control evidence is insufficient to determine whether that represents unsafe exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e3d31088c6fe4e0d","cmd-415f33944ec645c2","cmd-a8ebf618e1514a2e","cmd-14a33196bfc245ad","cmd-f8e6556570ac487b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All five material outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1 through node4: each node has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, different post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered relevant service, routing, data, and cluster state.","limitations":["Several combined command outputs were bounded or truncated. The conclusions therefore rely on redundant node-local API, SQL, routing, boot-identity, and lifecycle observations rather than unseen portions or executor summaries.","The lifecycle snapshots show Postgre